1. NOT A MEDICAL DEVICE
-----------------------
This is research software. It is NOT a medical device. It has NOT been cleared,
approved, or certified by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration or by any other
regulatory authority, and it MUST NOT be used to inform diagnosis, triage,
treatment, or any other care decision for an individual patient.

Tachypnea is a screening sign, not a diagnosis. A respiratory rate produced by
this software is an estimate from video and carries error that is documented,
age-dependent, and in the neonatal band severe: every camera-based extractor
evaluated in the accompanying work saturates near 30 breaths/min for true rates
of 60-80 breaths/min. Infants under two months are escalated to a contact or
radar measurement by design rather than screened. Anyone building on this work
should read the limitations section of the accompanying manuscript before
drawing conclusions from its outputs.


